      "title": "Some and Any",
      "objective": "Use some and any in affirmative, negative, and question contexts.",
      "description": "Some is common in affirmative statements and offers; any is common in negatives and most questions.",
      "content": "Put some before plural countable or uncountable nouns in positive statements. Use any after not and in information questions.",
      "examples": [
        "There are some apples.",
        "There isn't any bread.",
        "Do you have any rice?"
      ],
      "commonErrors": [
        "Do not use some in a normal negative statement.",
        "Do not forget the noun after some or any."
      ],
